<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39958" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestŭārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		quaestus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to gain</i>,
				<i>money-making</i>, <i>mercenary</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestuaria mancipia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 3, 2, 4, § 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulier,</span>”
				<i>a prostitute for hire</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 23, 2, 43, § 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">majestas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 13</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: quaestuaria, ae,
			f., <i>a prostitute</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex adulterā in quaestuariam versa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 6, 32, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
